        <headline>AOG SUPPORT - TSRV SYSTEMS</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: THIS AIRCRAFT IS CURRENTLY AOG DUE TO ENG #2 OVHT INDICATION ON TAKE-OFF. A SPIKE IN RH BLEED DUCT PRESSURE HAS BEEN NOTED AT THE START OF TAKE-OFF, REACHING 70 PSI.

ACTION:

1). OBSERVING ALL SAFETY PRECAUTIONS, GAIN ACCESS TO THE AIRCRAFT.

2). USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.

* RECORD RESULTS ON THE RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM.

** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM.

3). CHECK THE #2 HIGH STAGE REGULATOR FOR RUPTURED REVERSE FLOW DIAPHRAGM.

4). LEAK CHECK ALL HSR / HSV / PCCV AND BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY. PAY SPECIAL ATTENTION TO THE FOLLOWING SENSE LINES:
- HSR SUPPLY PRESSURE SENSE LINE
- HSV CONTROL PRESSURE SENSE LINE

5). REPLACE THE #2 HSR IAW AMM 36-11-07/401.

6). REPLACE THE #2 HSV IAW AMM 36-11-06/401.

7). RECORD ALL FINDINGS IN THIS WORK ORDER.

8). RETURN THE AIRCRAFT TO SERVICEABLE CONDITION.</description>
